+Google Cloud Universal Ledger (GCUL) (Google Cloud Platform)
+GCUL provides financial institutions and intermediaries with access to a
+managed, distributed ledger network and, by design, has certain distinct
+characteristics.
+1. Additional Definition.
+
+”Transaction” has the meaning given in the Service Specific Terms.
+”Transaction Data” means the Customer Data defined as Transaction
+Data in the Service Specific Terms.
+”Validator Nodes” has the meaning given in the Service Specific Terms.
+
+2. Amendments. This Addendum is amended as follows
+with respect to the Validator Nodes of GCUL:
+
+Section 3 (Duration) is replaced with the following:
+
+3. Duration. Regardless of whether the applicable Agreement
+has terminated or expired, this Addendum will remain in effect until, and
+automatically expire when, Google deletes all Customer Data (other than
+Transaction Data) as described in this Addendum.
+
+Section 6 (Data Deletion) is replaced with the following:
+
+6. Data Deletion. Customer acknowledges that (a) the
+functionality of the Services will not allow Customer to delete
+Transaction Data during the Term or Google to delete Transaction
+Data (including existing copies) from Google’s systems at the end of
+the Term, but that (b) the foregoing does not affect Customer’s ability
+to delete from systems managed or otherwise controlled by Customer any
+copies of, or information related to, Transaction Data at any time.
+
+Section 9.1 (Access; Rectification; Restricted Processing; Portability) is
+replaced with the following:
+
+Section 9.1 Access; Rectification; Restricted Processing;
+Portability. During the Term, Google will enable Customer, in a manner
+consistent with the functionality of the Services, to access and restrict
+processing of Transaction Data, and to export Transaction Data.
+If Customer becomes aware that any Transaction Data is inaccurate or
+outdated, Customer will be responsible for submitting a subsequent
+Transaction or other instruction to the Validator Node or using
+systems managed or otherwise controlled by Customer, to rectify or delete
+that data as appropriate.
+
+3. Customer Use Restriction. Customer acknowledges that
+Google does not require personal data in order to process, execute, and
+record Transactions on Validator Nodes and agrees that Customer will not
+include any personal data in Transaction Data.
